{"school":{"dbn":"17K770","name":"P.S. 770 New American Academy","boro":"Brooklyn","district":"17","district_label":"District 17","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Elementary","grades":"PK-5","status":"open","enrollment":274,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"60 EAST 94 STREET, BROOKLYN, NY 11212","phone":"718-221-5837","website":"WWW.PS770.ORG","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/kindergarten/64501","accessibility":"Partially Accessible","overview":"P.S. 770 is a unique and diverse choice elementary school in District 17. Due to being a choice school, families choose P.S. 770 from all over District 17 as well as neighboring districts in Brooklyn. Our school features and open classroom concept with teams of teachers that teacher every child. Starting in first grade, teams of teachers remain with your child from 1st-2nd grade and then 3rd-5th grade (looping model). Each grade in our school, K-5, has a Special Education Teacher (ICT on every grade) and we offer self contained (12:1:1) for K-2 and 3-5. Our unique model allows us to focus on every child and meet the needs of our diverse learners. All of our students are taught through our H.E.A.R.T.S. values and P.S. 770 has been identified as a Respect for All School for the past four years. All students at P.S. 770 receive PE, Music, and Dance and we provide 175 spots for free afterschool with Roads to Success. We also have partnerships with the Young People's Choir of New York City (YPC), CHAMPS, NYRR, and Music and the Brain. We pride ourselves on our focus on community, social/emotional learning, and joyous learning.","start_time":"8:15 AM","end_time":"3:05 PM","languages":"Spanish","subway":"3 to Sutter Av; 4 to Utica Av","bus":"B12, B14, B15, B17, B45, B46, B46-SBS, B47, B65","shared_building":"1","neighborhood":null,"latitude":40.6639,"longitude":-73.9279,"coordinate_source":"geocoded","first_year":"2015-16","last_year":"2024-25"},"series":{"attendance_inperson_k8_all"